**Convention 8.4 (outcome and cut discipline).** An absent literal address is
an actual legal Read reply. Stop carries the full terminal output and is not a
Read failure; the native trace's Event type has no Stop constructor. A finite
evaluator miss is local computation, not an executed external reject. An illegal
unexecuted operation has no event/successor and is represented by `none`.
An executed numerical reject is `some(reject,successor)`: the source is unchanged
but its request ordinal and actual row history advance. Busy cuts admit only
their prescribed next primitive transition. Whole-call claims are at idle macro
cuts; a proposed every-cut bridge must retain phase, pending response, cursor,
token and partial-delivery fields as well.

